  "revision": 22,
  "title": "indigo_agent_scripting: limit MERIDIAN_FLIP.USE_SOLVER to the solver exposure range",
  "description": "Follow-up of ticket 5e7ef4f3 (review note). Sequencer.js declares MERIDIAN_FLIP.USE_SOLVER with max 3600 s and publishes a numeric enable_meridian_flip() use_solver unchanged, but the solver agents limit AGENT_PLATESOLVER_EXPOSURE.EXPOSURE to 0..60 s (indigo_libs/indigo_platesolver.c ~line 1004), so e.g. enable_meridian_flip(120, 0) publishes 120 while the solver uses 60. Clamp the published USE_SOLVER and the stored solver exposure to the solver's 60 s maximum (as OFFSET is clamped to the Imager's -2..2 h), declare the item range 0..60, keep true/false behaviour unchanged, regenerate indigo_drivers/agent_scheduler/Sequencer.js.dat, add a test in indigo_test/integration/test_agent_scripting_sequencer.c (e.g. 120 publishes 60 and the flip sets 60), and update Sequencer.md, indigo_docs/mcp/agents/sequencer.md and indigo_docs/PROPERTIES.md.",
